WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Bran Stark: The Kingdom of the North,&nbsp;
the Kingdom of the Mountain and the Vale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:12.400
the Iron Islands, the Kingdom of the Rock, the&nbsp;
Kingdom of the Reach, the Stormlands, and Dorne.
&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.680
These regions had been established by&nbsp;
the First Men thousands of years before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.240
in the Age of Heroes.
One hero of this fabled age was Bran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:28.160
the Builder. Bran raised the Wall and built the&nbsp;
stronghold of Winterfell, establishing House Stark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.760
and reigning as the first King in the North.
Other legends tell of the Grey King in the Iron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.520
Islands. Grey King took a mermaid to wife&nbsp;
and defeated Nagga, the first sea dragon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.600
House Greyjoy of Pyke, the current rulers&nbsp;
of the region, claim to descend from him.
&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.480
House Casterly ruled the gold-rich Westerlands&nbsp;
from their mighty seat of Casterly Rock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.080
But their lands and power were swindled&nbsp;
from them by the legendary trickster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.440
Lann the Clever. The noble House of Lannister&nbsp;
is said to have descended from him.
&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.920
The verdant and fertile lands of the Reach were&nbsp;
first ruled by House Gardener. Its founder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.720
known as Garth Greenhand, wore a crown of&nbsp;
flowers and vines. He ruled from Highgarden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:22.880
as the first King of the Reach and was said&nbsp;
to have made the land bloom. Many noble houses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.000
trace their bloodlines back to him, including&nbsp;
the current lords of Highgarden, House Tyrell.
&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.480
In the Stormlands, according to ballads&nbsp;
of the age, a warrior named Durran fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.840
in love with Elenei, whose father was God of&nbsp;
the Sea, and mother was Goddess of the Wind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.240
She gave her maidenhead to him,&nbsp;
committing herself to a mortal life.
&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.880
Enraged, her parents called&nbsp;
upon the winds and waters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:55.680
destroying Durran's bayside keep and wiping out&nbsp;
his wedding gift. Durran declared war on the gods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:02.000
and rebuilt his keep, which was also destroyed.
Four more castles he raised, each stronger than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:09.200
the last. All fell to the power of the gods. But&nbsp;
Durran's seventh castle, Storm's End, withstood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:16.240
the gods' rage. Durran became known as Durran&nbsp;
Godsgrief and reigned as the first Storm King.
&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.880
There are countless other tales from the Age&nbsp;
of Heroes, too many to count. These histories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:28.560
weren't recorded in a book but passed down from&nbsp;
generation to generation through story and song.
&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.840
And while some of them may be dismissed&nbsp;
as fairy tales, every one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.080
Seven Kingdoms is defined by them.
The Starks of Winterfell trace their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:44.080
descent to the First Men in the Age of Heroes.
The family's founder was Brandon the Builder who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.920
in the aftermath of the Long Night,&nbsp;
helped establish the Night's Watch.
&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.320
Legend has it, he enlisted the aid of giants&nbsp;
and the powerful magic of the Children of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:59.440
the Forest to raise the mighty Wall, which&nbsp;
has protected the realm for generations.
&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.040
He went on to build the&nbsp;
ancestral seat of Winterfell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:08.400
and reigned as the first King in the North.
Robb Stark: The Starks reigned as kings for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.800
thousands of years, even withstanding the invasion&nbsp;
of the Andals. As the southern kingdoms fell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.680
and the Children were driven away,&nbsp;
the North stood strong, maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.320
its religious customs and its way of life.
Jon Snow: As for the other great Northern houses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.000
the Starks brought them into the&nbsp;
fold during the Age of Heroes.
&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.320
A Stark wrestled an ironborn for Bear&nbsp;
Island and gave it to the Mormonts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.080
A Stark granted a keep and land to a younger son,&nbsp;
Karlon, in return for putting down a rebellion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.280
His family then grew up into the Karstarks.
&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.600
Starks fought the wildlings and their&nbsp;
Kings-Beyond-the-Wall beside the Umbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:52.160
of Last Hearth, thus earning their fealty.
Boltons. Back then, they were the bane of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.840
the North. A few were even rumored to wear&nbsp;
their enemies' flayed skins as cloaks. 
&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.000
I've seen how the land stretches&nbsp;
much farther than any man knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.160
into the Land of Always Winter, where the&nbsp;
White Walkers came from during the Long Night.
&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.160
After the First Men and the Children&nbsp;
of the Forest beat them back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.080
Brandon the Builder raised the Wall&nbsp;
and set up the Night's Watch to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.880
guard the realms of men.
Sansa Stark: When Bran the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.360
Builder raised Winterfell and founded our&nbsp;
line, we were vassals to the Barrow Kings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.120
who claimed descent from the First King&nbsp;
and thus dominion over all the First Men.
&nbsp;

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.720
But after the Long Night, it was our house&nbsp;
who built the Wall and set the Night's Watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:36.800
to guard the realms of men whilst our king&nbsp;
sat in his barrow. My ancestors eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:42.160
revolted, waging what singers call the&nbsp;
Thousand Years War to free our lands.
&nbsp;

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:48.640
Other families joined us, recognizing that the&nbsp;
North is a cold and hard land and needed a king&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:54.880
who served its people before himself.&nbsp;
Finally, the last Barrow King bent the knee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:00.880
and House Stark became the Kings of Winter.
Tywin Lannister: We Lannisters claim our descent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.920
from the Andal invaders and, through&nbsp;
the female bloodline, Lann the Clever.
&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.320
According to the legend, Lann, using only&nbsp;
his wits, won Casterly Rock from the noble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:18.480
house of Casterly during the Age of Heroes.
Jaime Lannister: According to legend, a huntsman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.360
once tracked a lion that was terrorizing its&nbsp;
village all the way to its den. Though armed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.840
with only a spear, the man managed to kill both&nbsp;
the lion and its mate, but spared the cubs. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:35.040
mercy so pleased the Old Gods that they sent a&nbsp;
shaft of sunlight deep into the cave, gleaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:40.400
off golden walls. The hunter became a miner&nbsp;
and built a ringfort to guard his new wealth.
&nbsp;

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.920
Nobody ever asks what happened to the cubs. Maybe&nbsp;
the gods forgot about them, and they starved.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.320
Maybe there never were any cubs or&nbsp;
lions or hunter, doesn't matter.
&nbsp;

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:56.480
Someone found enough gold in that cave to buy&nbsp;
whatever truth he wanted, along with a castle that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:03.520
he'd name after his new family. Casterly Rock.
The castle is sadly all that remains of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:08.720
its namesake family, the Casterlys.&nbsp;
According to another legend, my ancestor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:14.240
Lann the Clever, swindled the castle from them.
The most common story is that he found a hidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:20.160
cleft in the rock and snuck into the castle.
As night, he whispered threats into sleeping ears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:25.680
howled in the darkness, planted one brother's&nbsp;
treasures in the room of another, and so forth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:31.040
By the end of his games, the Casterlys believed&nbsp;
a demon was haunting their home and fled.
&nbsp;

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.080
My brother prefers a different version. Lann the&nbsp;
Clever did find a secret entrance into the rock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.120
but used it to have his way&nbsp;
with the Casterly maidens.
&nbsp;

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:46.720
Eventually, the girls gave birth to golden-haired&nbsp;
bastards, and the Casterlys had no choice but to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:53.120
accept their father into the family. In gratitude,&nbsp;
he changed the family name to honor himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.840
and House Lannister was born.
Tywin Lannister: According to legend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:04.240
we trace their descent to Lann the Clever,&nbsp;
a trickster of the Dawn Age, who swindled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:11.360
the Casterlys out of Casterly Rock, their ancient&nbsp;
castle. A childish story, but not without merit.
&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.800
One, a mind can and should be&nbsp;
a weapon in a man's arsenal.
&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.720
Two, Lann must've been clever enough&nbsp;
not to rely solely on his wits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.920
After all, where today is House Casterly?
&nbsp;

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:33.360
Three, by keeping the Casterly name&nbsp;
on the castle, Lann reminded the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:37.840
of the price of getting in his way.
Catelyn Stark: The Arryns are direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:44.320
descendants of Andal invaders, who sailed across&nbsp;
the Narrow Sea and came ashore at the Fingers.
&nbsp;

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:52.800
According to legend, Ser Artys Arryn, known as&nbsp;
"the Winged Knight," soared through the skies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:57.280
atop a giant falcon, landing on&nbsp;
the peak of the highest mountain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:03.360
where he defeated the Griffin King in battle.
It was the Andals' first great victory over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:10.640
First Men. And Ser Artys was duly rewarded. He&nbsp;
was declared King of the Mountain and the Vale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:17.680
and the region renamed "the Vale of Arryn."
Robert Baratheon: The seat of House Baratheon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.560
is Storm's End, a legendary keep&nbsp;
raised in the Age of Heroes.
&nbsp;

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.960
It overlooks Shipbreaker Bay, where legend&nbsp;
has it that Durran, the first Storm King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:34.480
raised the keep with the aid of Bran the&nbsp;
Builder of House Stark, forging a centuries-long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:39.360
connection with the Stormlands and the North.
Brienne of Tarth: Even without our weather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:44.400
we have more than earned our name in&nbsp;
strife. The first Storm King, Durran,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:50.800
started his reign by declaring war on the gods&nbsp;
themselves. He loved the daughter of the sea god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:56.960
and the wind goddess, but they forbade the union.
At their wedding, the gods unleashed their might,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:01.200
pulling down his hold and killing all of&nbsp;
Durran's family and guests, though his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:08.640
wife shielded him. Durran vowed to rebuild, and&nbsp;
when he did, the gods again destroyed his home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.920
His councilors begged him to retreat&nbsp;
inland, but he would not abandon his war.
&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.600
Finally, with the council of the Children of&nbsp;
the Forest, or perhaps a young Bran the Builder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:25.840
Durran raised a seventh castle that, try as&nbsp;
they might and still do, the wind and sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:33.360
gods could not tear asunder. Durran took the name&nbsp;
Godsgrief and called his new home Storm's End.
&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:38.720
Samwell Tarly: According to legend, House&nbsp;
Targaryen survived the Doom of Valyria thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.520
Daenys the Dreamer, who foresaw the calamity&nbsp;
and convinced her father to flee their homeland.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:49.840
It could be true. The Targaryens&nbsp;
were always a bit more.

